                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ludo is a classic board game which has been derived from the classic Indian game, pachisi. It is simpler than the pachisi. It is a game that has been designed for between two and four players but I've always felt that the more that you have the better the game is. Variations of Ludo include the popular board games Sorry!, Aggravation and Trouble.\n\nThe good news is that everything works as it was intended. The game plays smoothly and correctly. If you're a fan of ludo and don't have anybody to play with locally you're going to be able to play a game against the computer AI. That works fine.\n\nThe problem that I have with the game is that it supports local multiplayer only. There is no online. This is a major downer. You can easily find the board game in most children's toy stores or you can opt to play the variants which are again easily accessible. You're much better off getting a copy of the physical game and playing your friends or family live if you intend to play against them.\n\nUnfortunately, playing against the computer AI can become rather tedious and boring quickly especially when you have other games that you can play.\n\nThis is one purely for the hardcore Ludo fans.\n\nFor more reviews and our popular giveaways please visit [url=http://www.steamified.com/]Steamified[/url]",
